const vlsiProjects=[{name:`4-bit Palindrome Detector`,tags:[`Verilog`,`FSM`],blurb:`Sequence-detection logic built as a finite state machine to identify 4-bit palindromic patterns on a serial input stream.`,problem:`Detect palindromic 4-bit sequences on a serial bitstream without buffering the whole word externally.`,architecture:`A Moore-style FSM tracks the incoming bit pattern across states, comparing early and late bits as they arrive.`,implementation:`Implemented in Verilog with a compact state register and next-state logic, simulated for functional correctness.`,verification:`Verified with directed testcases covering palindromic and non-palindromic sequences.`,learning:`Reinforced FSM design fundamentals and how state encoding choices affect readability and timing.`},{name:`Smart Radar System`,tags:[`Arduino`,`Embedded`,`Sensors`],blurb:`An embedded distance-sensing system built around an ultrasonic sensor and servo sweep to visualise nearby objects.`,problem:`Build a low-cost radar-style system that can detect and visualise objects across a sweep angle.`,architecture:`An ultrasonic sensor mounted on a servo sweeps across a range, with the microcontroller reading distance at each angle.`,implementation:`Programmed on Arduino, reading ultrasonic pulses and driving the servo sweep, with data sent out for visualisation.`,verification:`Tested by sweeping across objects at known distances and angles to confirm consistent readings.`,learning:`Hands-on experience combining sensor timing, actuator control, and real-time data handling on embedded hardware.`},{name:`6 DOF Robotic Arm`,tags:[`Arduino`,`Servo Control`,`Embedded`],blurb:`A six degrees-of-freedom robotic arm built with servo motors and microcontroller-driven joint control.`,problem:`Control six independent joints smoothly and predictably from a single microcontroller.`,architecture:`Each joint is driven by a servo motor, coordinated through a central control loop that maps target positions to servo angles.`,implementation:`Built on Arduino with PWM-based servo control and a simple command interface for positioning each joint.`,verification:`Verified through manual joint-by-joint movement tests and repeatability checks on target positions.`,learning:`Deepened understanding of multi-actuator coordination and the practical limits of hobby servo precision.`},{name:`32-bit RV32I Processor`,tags:[`SystemVerilog`,`RISC-V`,`FPGA`],blurb:`A pipelined 32-bit RISC-V processor supporting the RV32I instruction set, with hazard detection and forwarding.`,problem:`Implement a functionally correct pipelined processor for the RV32I instruction set.`,architecture:`Classic 5-stage pipeline (fetch, decode, execute, memory, writeback) with forwarding paths and hazard detection.`,implementation:`Written in SystemVerilog, targeting FPGA implementation with modular, testable stage boundaries.`,verification:`Verified against RV32I instruction behaviour using directed and self-checking testbenches.`,learning:`Practical experience with pipelining trade-offs — hazards, forwarding, and control complexity.`},{name:`UVM Testbench Suite`,tags:[`UVM`,`Python`],blurb:`A constrained-random verification environment with automated regression scripts for high-speed serial interface modules.`,problem:`Build a reusable, scalable verification environment instead of relying on ad-hoc directed tests.`,architecture:`Standard UVM environment: driver, monitor, scoreboard, and sequences layered over a constrained-random stimulus generator.`,implementation:`UVM components in SystemVerilog with Python scripts to automate regression runs and log triage.`,verification:`Coverage-driven — regression run across constrained-random sequences with functional coverage tracking.`,learning:`Learned how reusable verification infrastructure pays off across multiple related interface modules.`}],leadershipEvents=[{year:`2025`,name:`Arduino Workshop`,role:`Coordinator`,desc:`Hands-on workshop introducing students to Arduino fundamentals and embedded projects.`},{year:`2025`,name:`Flyer Making Competition`,role:`Coordinator`,desc:`Creative design competition run for the student community.`},{year:`2025`,name:`C-Race`,role:`Coordinator`,desc:`Competitive programming event focused on C fundamentals.`},{year:`2025`,name:`Startup Autopsy`,role:`Coordinator`,desc:`Session breaking down real startup case studies for students.`},{year:`2025`,name:`IOTvate`,role:`Coordinator`,desc:`IoT-focused ideation and building event for student teams.`},{year:`2025`,name:`Creovate`,role:`Coordinator`,desc:`Creative-technical event blending design and engineering challenges.`},{year:``,name:`Other Technical Events`,role:`Coordinator — Digital Nexus`,desc:`Additional workshops, competitions, and sessions organised through Digital Nexus.`}],journey=[`ECE Journey`,`Arduino / Embedded Projects`,`Digital Nexus`,`Video Editing`,`Verilog / SystemVerilog`,`RTL / VLSI`,`Current Goal: Digital IC Design`],eventGallery=[{name:`Digital Nexus`,desc:`Working together to organise technical events, workshops and creative opportunities for the student community.`,image:`https://res.cloudinary.com/dmnxhbzke/image/upload/v1788691857/WhatsApp_Image_2025-08-22_at_23.16.10_epim4b.jpg`,alt:`Digital Nexus student community`,real:!0},{name:`Arduino Workshop`,desc:`A hands-on introduction to Arduino fundamentals, components and embedded project building.`},{name:`Creovate`,desc:`A creative-technical event bringing students together through design and engineering challenges.`},{name:`IOTvate`,desc:`An IoT-focused ideation and building event for student teams.`},{name:`Flyer Making Competition`,desc:`A creative design competition encouraging visual communication and student participation.`},{name:`Startup Autopsy`,desc:`A session exploring real startup case studies and the decisions behind them.`}];window.PortfolioData={vlsiProjects,leadershipEvents,journey,eventGallery};